  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 335 AM CDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nLooking into the weekend, ensemble guidance continues to\nindicate a continuance of heat and humidity into at least\nSaturday. NBM guidance provides a 60-90% chance of high\ntemperatures Saturday being 95 F or higher along with a 40-50%\nchance of dewpoints being greater than 70 F along I-70 and south\nboth Saturday and Sunday. Heat headlines were not extended into\nSunday due to some uncertainty in the exact timing of a cold\nfront Sunday into Monday, but also a chance of another\nconvective system. A few deterministic models do present similar\nsynoptic patterns that could allow for a repeat of yesterday and\ntoday to occur Saturday night and into Sunday: a ridge-running\nconvective system that may cast clouds and outflow over parts of\nthe region. If that were to occur, then temperatures on Sunday\ncould be low enough to not necessitate heat headlines.\n\nOn the brighter side, ensemble guidance is continuing to show\nstrong signs of a cold front moving through the region at the\nbeginning of next week, bringing temperatures and humidity\ncloser to seasonal normals. Cluster analysis is in agreement\nthat heights will fall and bring in northerly flow starting\nSunday night into Monday. How long this cool down will last is\nuncertain. Beyond Tuesday, guidance indicates a range of\npossibilities. On one hand another ridge could build far north\nover the central CONUS bringing another hot and humid air mass,\nwhile on the other hand a weaker ridge to the southwest could\noccur that may allow for an additional cold front to keep\ntemperatures near normal. As a result, both the LREF and NBM\nhave a 10-15 degree spread in their high temperatures for\nWednesday and beyond.",
